<title>ESTONIA: TALLINNA TO DISCUSS PROFIT REVISION.</title>
<headline>TALLINNA TO DISCUSS PROFIT REVISION.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tallinna Pank's council will on July 14 discuss a possible revision of its 1997 net profit forecast, it said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not raise the profit forecast before the board has discussed it,&quot; the bank's deputy chairman Targo Raus told a news conference.</p>
<p>Raus added he would not speculate on how probable a revision would be.</p>
<p>Tallinna Pank's six months net profit was 32.6 million kroons, 45.6 percent of its 71.5 million kroons annual profit forecast.</p>
<p>Board member Martti Siimann said the bank has exceeded the profit forecast by five million kroons as of the end of June.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
